e  was in the house of course hey  we didn't quit you quit i came here and  i felt you know really guilty about  everything that i had driving through  this town i  went back to my hotel room and i sat  there and i just like cried  and i realized that everything i have is  is a privilege and that you know i feel  that one of the reasons hopefully  you know god gave me what i have is that  he realizes i'm not going to take  advantage of the gifts  by 1985 tom was making all the right  moves to become the top gun that he is  today a three-time oscar nominee worth a  reported 600 million dollars and we were  with him every step of the way right now  i'm getting involved over the past  couple of years  more involvement in the overall process  of film in terms of developing  the script it's all been very calculated  i mean i really take my time in choosing  the films that i do and the people who i  get involved with and the great thing  about success is that  that i have the freedom in the room to  do that and i'm really taking advantage  of that i mean i researched this role  for two months  before i decided to do it  you know and i feel very thankful for  that luxury and that success  i've been having nightmares that no one  would show up except for my parents and  my girlfriend  but uh so i want to thank you all very  much how do you keep from becoming cocky  life is a humbling experience i don't  know how else to say it  if you want me to stop or you want to  give me any signal uh  grab my arm  [Applause]  the hand prints are now in i wasn't sure  if anyone was going to show up  [Applause]  it's a sexy  thing being a vampire tom also proved  two leading men can be better than one  when he shared the screen with brad pitt  in interview with the vampire i watched  this guy and he was fired  he was just fire  you know he took his  his stuff and he took it to another  level he took another direction i think  that's fantastic in london i rented a  go-kart track and we invited everyone in  brad and everybody came we just drove  around the track and just went nuts with  these go-karts and it was great after  that tom took a bite out of producing  his first movie in 1996 turning the 60s  tv show into a billion dollar franchise  [Music]  i thought man what we could do you know  this great theme music  and i just thought man i could just  picture the the trailer you know and  this story this has been a dream of mine  as a kid you know when i used to go to  movies it's you know now i'm making them  and i'm producing them and it's it is a  real pie  and we were there when he got braces at  age 40. it's not that bad actually it's  just to push these teeth out so that i  can close my mouth  that's how you know i didn't realize  that you could actually close your mouth  all the way plus we learned things like  tom's a hopeless romantic i like  relationships i enjoy the  the complexity and the  uh  intimacy of that what's your idea of the  perfect romantic night  definitely  uh you know candles come into play you  know  nice music  a beautiful walk under this moonlit  night or sunset on the beach  down to a picnic  those kind of things i i really love  along the way mr cruz gave us some of  the most iconic lines in movie history  portia  there is no substitute i want the truth  you can't handle the truth  you  complete me  it's so  amazing to me that  when you do something and then to hear  people say it back to you you complete  me i feel the need the need for speed up  if a lot of guys have used that  when you first came into the business  you gave yourself 10 years to make it i  think i've done all right  i just  love making movies i love what i do i  can't believe where i've come from in  the past since the beginning i mean when  i started out i know absolutely  nothing about really acting or you know  i just wanted to be an actor in looking  back i'm i kind of go wow i've you know  done i've done well there's that point  where you go that